{
  "$comment": "DESIGN.md \u00a76.1. Forms are geometry and attachment topology and nothing else \u2014 'rules about shape, not content'. No form here knows what it will be made of, and none carries a statistic: mass, swing speed, impulse profile and durability are all derived at the point of use from the materials that end up in the slots. The \u00a76.1 target is ~60 forms; M1 needs melee and bodies, so these are the ones that exist. Each part also carries a top-down `offset` in the form's own frame: +x is the direction the wielder faces, +y is to its right. That is geometry, so it lives with the form rather than in a renderer.",
